In this example T must extend Number and implement Comparable<T> which should ﬁt all "normal" built-in number
implementations like Integer or BigDecimal but doesn't ﬁt the more exotic ones like Striped64.
Since multiple inheritance is not allowed, you can use at most one class as a bound and it must be the ﬁrst listed.
For example, <T extends Comparable<T> & Number> is not allowed because Comparable is an interface, and not a
