Interestingly, this will print "same", even though we are testing the strings the wrong way. Why is that? Because the
Java Language Speciﬁcation (Section 3.10.5: String Literals) stipulates that any two string >>literals<< consisting of
the same characters will actually be represented by the same Java object. Hence, the == test will give true for equal
literals. (The string literals are "interned" and added to a shared "string pool" when your code is loaded, but that is
actually an implementation detail.)

