Section 131.5: Pitfall - Directly subclassing `Throwable`
Throwable has two direct subclasses, Exception and Error. While it's possible to create a new class that extends
Throwable directly, this is inadvisable as many applications assume only Exception and Error exist.
More to the point there is no practical beneﬁt to directly subclassing Throwable, as the resulting class is, in eﬀect,
simply a checked exception. Subclassing Exception instead will result in the same behavior, but will more clearly
convey your intent.
